  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will gradually build into the region Wednesday \ninto the Labor Day weekend. This will bring a warmer, drier pattern \nto the region. Guidance remains in strong agreement on an upper \nridge center building over the region Friday and Saturday. This will \nbring much above average temperatures by Friday and Saturday into \nthe mid and upper 90s. NBM 90th percentile high temperatures for \nSaturday through Monday are in the upper 90s to around 100. This is \npossible, given the strength of the upper ridge nearing 5970 meters \nby Sunday and Monday, shown by the GFS. The ECMWF shows a weaker \nupper ridge. As a result, forecast highs are currently in the upper \n80s to lower 90s by Sunday and Monday, given an increasing \nspread in the strength of the upper ridge. \n\nThe stronger upper level ridging will also keep precipitation \nchances fairly limited Wednesday through the Labor Day weekend. \nLatest NBM guidance does still keep some slight chance PoPs, \ngenerally less than 20 percent, Wednesday night, and again during \nthe evening and overnight Friday through Sunday. However, based on \nensemble guidance, precipitation would be light. Latest ensemble \nguidance continues to show a less than 20 percent chance of \nprecipitation exceeding one tenth of an inch Wednesday night and \nagain into the weekend.",
